### Use platform plugins in background isolates with Dart

Source: https://docs.flutter.dev/perf/isolates.md

Pass a RootIsolateToken to a spawned isolate and call BackgroundIsolateBinaryMessenger.ensureInitialized to enable platform channel communication.

```dart
import 'dart:isolate';

import 'package:flutter/services.dart';
import 'package:shared_preferences/shared_preferences.dart';

void main() {
  // Identify the root isolate to pass to the background isolate.
  RootIsolateToken rootIsolateToken = RootIsolateToken.instance!;
  Isolate.spawn(_isolateMain, rootIsolateToken);
}

Future<void> _isolateMain(RootIsolateToken rootIsolateToken) async {
  // Register the background isolate with the root isolate.
  BackgroundIsolateBinaryMessenger.ensureInitialized(rootIsolateToken);

  // You can now use the shared_preferences plugin.
  SharedPreferences sharedPreferences = await SharedPreferences.getInstance();

  print(sharedPreferences.getBool('isDebug'));
}
```

